  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AEV">Situation <span data-tag="0AEV">81.10.6</span>.</a> Here $S$ is a base scheme, $f : Y \to X$ is a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$, and $Z \to X$ is a closed immersion of finite presentation. We assume that $f^{-1}(Z) \to Z$ is an isomorphism and that $f$ is flat in every point $x \in |f^{-1}Z|$. We set $U = X \setminus Z$ and $V = Y \setminus f^{-1}(Z)$. Picture </p>
